Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/Albrhi-Repo
Description: Save any moment, and keep Locket from reporting your phone as jailbroken. Arabic or English.
 .
 ▍SAVE A MOMENT
 A friend’s photo or video, saved to your Photos at full size — the one they actually sent,
 not a screenshot. Hold two fingers anywhere in Locket, and every moment it has loaded is
 listed, newest first; tap one to save it. It saves what is already on your phone, and does
 not touch anything you would pay Locket for.
 .
 ▍HIDES THE JAILBREAK
 Locket does not block a jailbroken phone, but it does tell three companies your phone is
 one: its analytics, its ad attribution, and its crash reporting each run their own check
 and send the answer home. On a modified device that answer can quietly count against your
 account. This tweak makes those checks come back clean.
 .
 ▍HOW IT WORKS
 The checks all ask the system the same few questions — is this file here, can this app be
 opened, is this folder writable. This sits underneath and answers only those questions,
 only for the handful of paths a jailbreak check looks at. Everything else the app asks the
 system passes straight through untouched.
 .
 ▍WHAT IT DOES NOT DO
 It does not touch payments, subscriptions or anything you would pay Locket for. A tool that
 unlocks paid features by faking a subscription was reviewed and deliberately not built —
 that is taking money from the people who make the app, not a device tweak.
 .
 ▍SEE WHAT IT CAUGHT
 Hold two fingers anywhere in Locket for a small screen that says how many checks were
 answered and which ones. Arabic and English.
 .
 TESTED ON Locket 2.46.1. Nothing is pinned to a version number.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source under the GNU GPL v3.
